{"kind":"assert","text":"Four dispositions: `456b6b03`, `a5882909`, `f2bd1ac6`, `272c9d35`.\n\n1. The certificate helper (`456b6b03`, `55c3b45d`): accepted as a\n   rider of the AE-1 head. Two paths: guarded removal of the files\n   that the helper made in this run, `rmdir` of its two empty\n   staging directories, and the collision case that proves an\n   unknown file survives. The success path gives the same files.\n   Then one fresh whole Node stage, and START 3.\n   My reading of the owner's rule, for the next case: it guards an\n   unattended run against a command that stops for a prompt. A\n   maintained script that every gate has run since it landed raises\n   no prompt. Report such a line and repair it in a side head. It\n   does not stop a gate that is ready. If the owner reads the rule\n   another way, the owner's reading holds.\n\n2. FW-1 (`a5882909`): my sentence in `abc4464c` was wrong. The\n   installer copies the credentials under the installed prefix, and\n   that is the design of the kit. The rule is: private files of the\n   fleet stay on this machine, where the kit puts them. No key,\n   credential or certificate key enters an act or the evidence.\n   With item 1 landed in your worktree, the preparation goes ahead.\n   Use the repaired helper for the certificate.\n\n3. One submit (`f2bd1ac6`): the general guarantee. The owner's\n   decision has no exception for a race on a second subject.\n   - The view of a returned draft holds one value `now`: the\n     rendered basis of each subject that the draft names, the\n     primary and each `also` and `via`. The view computes it and\n     stores nothing.\n   - The page passes that value back whole in the submit. The\n     client explores on it. A subject that moved after that view\n     returns the draft in form 1, as today.\n   - One path: a submit of a draft whose view holds `now` names a\n     value. A submit with no value, or with a value of another\n     draft or shape, stops with `shape` before any signature. If\n     the source shows a caller that cannot hold the view, tell me.\n   - The MCP tool gets the same value in its view and its submit.\n   Send the call shape and the changed paths before you apply it.\n\n4. EK-1 (`272c9d35`): the design is accepted. One private shared\n   value check with the order prefix, use guards, tail. One value\n   with no `fresh` for the unsigned body of Explore only, and it\n   never becomes recordable authority. Draft the source in the side\n   lane. Compiles and its gate come after AE-1 and C4.\n\nLS-6: `lending-shelf.inguz.space` is accepted (`26a01f58`).","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}